{"id": "EUVD-2026-76584", "enisaUuid": "02a1e971-9756-38a2-9493-716abbc4faac", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: gate nfs2 setacl by argp->mask\n\nThe NFSACL v2 SETACL path shares the decoder convention used by its\nv3 sibling: nfsaclsvc_decode_setaclargs() fills in argp->acl_access\nonly when NFS_ACL is set in the request mask and argp->acl_default\nonly when NFS_DFACL is set, leaving the other pointer NULL because\nthe argument buffer is zeroed up to pc_argzero before decode.\n\nnfsacld_proc_setacl() then hands both pointers to set_posix_acl()\nunconditionally. set_posix_acl(idmap, dentry, type, NULL) is the VFS\n\"remove this ACL type\" operation, so an omitted arm is\nindistinguishable from an explicit request to delete that ACL. A\nSETACL carrying only NFS_ACL silently strips the directory's default\nACL; mask=0 strips both.\n\nThis is the same defect just fixed in nfsd3_proc_setacl(); apply the\nsame remedy. Gate each set_posix_acl() call on its mask bit and\ninitialize error to 0 so that a request with neither bit set leaves\nthe on-disk ACLs untouched and returns success. The out_drop_lock\npath and the unconditional posix_acl_release() in\nnfsaclsvc_release_setacl() already tolerate the skipped arms.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:45", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e4422b05f410f95c51b68a0db4bf1d87f6d22f5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e41d173d9dc735cecb15ab7aa63ecab09338f81b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f951b22dbeec46f2e0fba81cb80d1b0c686b61eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/37eea38e7898538f0ec5f1eb8b18d8646e4be41c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3a7e20ed66d3f04d37883c398da8a113b430769"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89672", "GHSA-cpgj-m749-r929"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e9abb3c-4d49-333f-a86e-f2c61d8cc395", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "125ed79d-e251-3fdc-a31c-75cc57c49231", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a257cdd0e2179630d3201c32ba14d7fcb3c3a055 <a3a7e20ed66d3f04d37883c398da8a113b430769"}, {"id": "32c4f139-4d30-3275-ad28-7ace02068541", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a257cdd0e2179630d3201c32ba14d7fcb3c3a055 <f951b22dbeec46f2e0fba81cb80d1b0c686b61eb"}, {"id": "3517020d-7889-3dc7-b240-04f5012d672b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3b96d4e3-1639-391c-bf4c-08e14e59dff3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.13"}, {"id": "56beb13e-404c-31ce-a56b-31ba731d2a45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a257cdd0e2179630d3201c32ba14d7fcb3c3a055 <37eea38e7898538f0ec5f1eb8b18d8646e4be41c"}, {"id": "6bffe03b-c2d7-35e8-81a4-d335ddf87c6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a257cdd0e2179630d3201c32ba14d7fcb3c3a055 <e41d173d9dc735cecb15ab7aa63ecab09338f81b"}, {"id": "768072fc-36e0-3a56-8a67-0d53fb877e5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a257cdd0e2179630d3201c32ba14d7fcb3c3a055 <8e4422b05f410f95c51b68a0db4bf1d87f6d22f5"}, {"id": "c4c3f6ab-ca86-3830-a88f-0718465493af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "da539a76-c1ca-3587-b4e4-c26fbb9a1c5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "f54a0065-b87a-33e2-8ebc-c103509f6dad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "ffe8ea64-e9e4-3d0b-8321-84621aec8d6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produ